      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a predictive model for residential larceny risks in the Midwest. I've been looking at some recent census updates for a few specific ZIP codes in the urban periphery where we've seen a spike in theft reports. I want to see if there's a statistical correlation between the changing ethnic composition of these neighborhoods and the rising crime rates. Can you help me walk through how to analyze if these demographic shifts are significant predictors for our risk assessment?",
